WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.520
A love letter.

2
00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:04.760
One line, then another, then another.

3
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.440
It keeps growing.

4
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.860
Then two hands fold it
down into a neat box.

5
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:13.210
A counter ticks up to 14, and stops.

6
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:17.710
The first line reads: "Shall I
compare thee to a summer’s day?"

7
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.560
So much love, and only
fourteen lines to hold it.

8
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.530
Why would a poet choose
a space that tight?

9
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.400
In this mission, you'll
learn to count the beat:

10
00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.990
ten syllables and five stresses.

11
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:33.900
You'll meet the two shapes of
sonnet: an octave and a sestet,

12
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.390
or three quatrains and a couplet.

13
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:41.100
And you'll ask what a fixed shape lets
a poet do that a long letter can't.

14
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:46.040
Your mission: work out why a poet
squeezes love into fourteen lines.
